BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:state-pte-florida-2025-04-01@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T115707Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250402
SUMMARY:Florida: F-1065 due
DESCRIPTION:Florida partnership information return is a required filing und
 er specified conditions (e.g. a partnership with a corporate partner) even 
 though Florida has no personal income tax and a pure partnership generally 
 owes no Florida tax itself. | Florida partnership information return is a r
 equired filing under specified conditions (e.g. a partnership with a corpor
 ate partner) even though Florida has no personal income tax and a pure part
 nership generally owes no Florida tax itself. File Form F-7004 by the origi
 nal due date\; automatic approval if a federal extension was obtained (only
  one extension permitted\; approx. 6 months). | Authority: Florida Departme
 nt of Revenue\, Form F-1065 instructions\, direct fetch this session from f
 loridarevenue.com's own PDF: "You must file Florida Form F-1065 on or befor
 e the first day of the fourth month following the close of your taxable yea
 r" - i.e. April 1 for a calendar-year filer\, not the 15th-of-month pattern
  most other states use. (This corrects an earlier same-session finding of "
 May 1" that had come from a third-party mirror rather than floridarevenue.c
 om directly.) | Source: https://floridarevenue.com/forms_library/current/f1
 065.pdf | This date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not reflect 
 a later-announced change\; confirm against the cited source before relying 
 on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
